 See the [API reference documentation](https://docs.page/invertase/denque/api) for more examples.
 
+## API
+
+### `rotate(steps = 1)`
+
+Rotates the queue in place and returns the same queue. Positive `steps` move
+values from the back to the front; negative `steps` move values from the front
+to the back. Counts are finite integers and are normalized modulo the current
+queue length. Empty and single-item queues are unchanged.
+
+```js
+const denque = new Denque([1, 2, 3, 4]);
+denque.rotate();       // [4, 1, 2, 3]
+denque.rotate(-2);     // [1, 2, 3, 4]
+```
+
+Passing a non-number, non-finite number, or non-integer throws an `Error`.
+
